--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the operation of the RX TCP offload engine, with IP frames
-- with SNAP and ethernet encapsulation, which have good IP checksum but are
-- not TCP or UDP frames.
-- This test is run in gigabit TBI FIFO mode.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks that the IP header checksum logic can recognised good checksums.
-- * Checks that the TOE recognises that these are not TCP or UDP frames
--   and therefore does not attempt to check the TCP/UDP checksum.
-- * Checks that the TOE can recognise both ethernet and SNAP encapsulation.
-- * Checks that the GEM can correctly report different types of encapsulation
--   and IP frames.
-- * Checks that the external filter interface can correctly extract 
--   IP addresses.
--
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in TBI mode into a 32-bit FIFO data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames with either SNAP or ethernet encapsulation, which
--     have good IP checksum but are not checked for TCP or UDP.
--
-- Test 1.1
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with VLAN tag with no CFI bit.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.2
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 1.3
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with VLAN and SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 1.4 
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with neither VLAN nor SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.5
--    Broadcast frame, IP Fragmentation (MF bit set), otherwise valid 
--    IP and TCP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.6
--    Broadcast frame, IP Fragmentation (Fragment offset non zero), 
--    otherwise valid IP and TCP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.7
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with neither VLAN nor SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
--
--  4. Check statistics for correct values from above tests.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states 0
bus_grant_delay 0


--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in TBI mode into a 32-bit FIFO data bus.
--******************************************************************************
-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd     200 00009040  -- check value of pcs control register
apbwr     200 00000040  -- disable autonegotioation
apbrd     200 00008040  -- check autoneg disabled
apbwr      04 01080c01  -- enable RX TCP offload engine. and TBI mode, 32 bit.
apbrd      04 01080c01  -- verify write to network config register.
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive

apbrd(int) 24 00000200  -- check link status change interrupt


